ression $0.45x$ represents $45\\%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $45\\%$ of all students from last year are now in the science club." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186609857 1071 "Last year, a farm produced $400$ kilograms of oranges. This year, production is $125%$ greater than last year. How many kilograms of oranges did the farm produce this year?\n\nThe farm produced\n{{field-1}}\nkilograms of oranges this year." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186609857 1071 "Last year, a farm produced $400$ kilograms of oranges. This year, production is $125\\%$ greater than last year. How many kilograms of oranges did the farm produce this year?\n\nThe farm produced\n{{field-1}}\nkilograms of oranges this year." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186609857 1074 "To find this year's orange production, we apply a $125%$ increase to last year's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $125%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+125%=225%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n225%=\\frac{225}{100}=2.25\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original amount by $2.25:$\n\n$$\n400\\times 2.25=900\n$$\n\nSo, the farm produced $900$ kilograms of oranges this year." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186609857 1074 "To find this year's orange production, we apply a $125\\%$ increase to last year's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $125\\%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100\\%+125\\%=225\\%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n225\\%=\\frac{225}{100}=2.25\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original amount by $2.25:$\n\n$$\n400\\times 2.25=900\n$$\n\nSo, the farm produced $900$ kilograms of oranges this year." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186609858 1071 "Find $120%$ of $90,$ and then $140%$ of the result." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186609858 1071 "Find $120\\%$ of $90,$ and then $140\\%$ of the result." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186609858 1074 "First, we find $120%$ of $90:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}120%\\times 90 & =\\frac{120}{100}\\times 90 \\\\  & =1.2\\times 90 \\\\  & =108\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find $140%$ of the result $(108):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}140%\\times 108 & =\\frac{140}{100}\\times 108 \\\\  & =1.4\\times 108 \\\\  & =151.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $151.2.$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186609858 1074 "First, we find $120\\%$ of $90:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}120\\%\\times 90 & =\\frac{120}{100}\\times 90 \\\\  & =1.2\\times 90 \\\\  & =108\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find $140\\%$ of the result $(108):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}140\\%\\times 108 & =\\frac{140}{100}\\times 108 \\\\  & =1.4\\times 108 \\\\  & =151.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $151.2.$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186609859 1071 "A toy store sold $250$ puzzles in June. In July, sales are $140%$ greater than in June. How many puzzles did the toy store sell in July?\n\nThe toy store sold\n{{field-1}}\npuzzles in July." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186609859 1071 "A toy store sold $250$ puzzles in June. In July, sales are $140\\%$ greater than in June. How many puzzles did the toy store sell in July?\n\nThe toy store sold\n{{field-1}}\npuzzles in July." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186609859 1074 "To find July's sales, we apply a $140%$ increase to June's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $140%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+140%=240%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n240%=\\frac{240}{100}=2.4\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original amount by $2.4:$\n\n$$\n250\\times 2.4=600\n$$\n\nSo, the toy store sold $600$ puzzles in July." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186609859 1074 "To find July's sales, we apply a $140\\%$ increase to June's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $140\\%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100\\%+140\\%=240\\%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the