ity that the $5$th picked crayon is the first green crayon is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =f(5) \\\\  & =(0.85)^{5-1}(0.15) \\\\  & =(0.85)^{4}(0.15) \\\\  & ≈0.078\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186630185 1071 "A particular town started with $67\\,000$ inhabitants. The population, $P$ of the town after $t$ years, is given by the formula\n\n$$\nP=67\\,000\\cdot (\\text{___})^{t}.\n$$\n\nIf the population of the town reduces at a rate of $4%$ per year, then what is the missing value in the expression for $P?$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186630185 1071 "A particular town started with $67\\,000$ inhabitants. The population, $P$ of the town after $t$ years, is given by the formula\n\n$$\nP=67\\,000\\cdot (\\text{___})^{t}.\n$$\n\nIf the population of the town reduces at a rate of $4\\%$ per year, then what is the missing value in the expression for $P?$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186630185 1074 "The population of the town reduces at a rate of $4%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay rate $r$) is:\n\n$$\ny(t)=a(1-r)^{t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=67\\,000$ is the initial number of inhabitants.\n\n- $r=0.04$ is the decay rate ($4%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in years.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $P$ is\n\n$$\np(t)=67\\,000\\cdot (1-0.04)^{t}=67\\,000\\cdot (0.96)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $0.96.$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186630185 1074 "The population of the town reduces at a rate of $4\\%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay rate $r$) is:\n\n$$\ny(t)=a(1-r)^{t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=67\\,000$ is the initial number of inhabitants.\n\n- $r=0.04$ is the decay rate ($4\\%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in years.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $P$ is\n\n$$\np(t)=67\\,000\\cdot (1-0.04)^{t}=67\\